# CheckMed — SwiftData writes and merges

A no-op `@Model` assignment still invalidates SwiftUI. Never assign if the value is unchanged.

```swift
if existing.status != incoming.status {
    existing.status = incoming.status
}
```

Apply to **every** `@Model` (DoseLog, Medicine, Treatment, refill, report, Phil, settings). Especially merge/sync: do not write `pending → pending` or `missed → missed`.

`get` / `fetch` / `load` / `calculate` / `summary` / `adherence` / `streak` / `count` must not hide writes. If repair is needed, use a separate explicit mutation.

Operations that can run more than once (sync, merge, seed, reconcile, dose generation, reminders, import) must be idempotent: no duplicate medicines, logs, alarms, or extra writes.

**Doses:** do not invent historical missed logs from an old Rx document date. Treatment start must be explicit. Do not recreate existing dose events on launch, sync, navigation, or login.

Canonical flow (one source of truth): Prescription → Medicine → Treatment/Schedule → DoseLog → Adherence → Refill → Journey → Report. Do not give Home/Report/Phil/Refill competing copies of the same lists.
